          %h2#idea Idea
          %ul
            %li
              %p A category consists of a collection of things and binary relationships (or transitions) between them, such that these relationships can be combined and include the “identity” relationship “is the same as.”
            %li
              %p
                A category is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
                (a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
                with multiple edges) with a rule saying how to
                %em compose
                two edges that fit together to get a new edge. Furthermore, each vertex has an edge starting and ending at that vertex, which acts as an identity for this composition.
            %li
              %p
                A category is a combinatorial model for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space"} directed space
                – a “directed
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-type"} homotopy 1-type
                = succeed "," do
                  %em objects
                = succeed "." do
                  %em morphisms
            %li
              %p
                More precisely, a category consists of a collection of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
                and a collection of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
                object and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
                object. If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is a morphism with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                as its source and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                as its target, we write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
              %p
                and we say that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is a morphism from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} compose
                a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : x \to y
                and a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : y \to z
                to get a morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g : x \to z
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AssociativityDiagram.png", :width => "400"}/
          %p
            A good example to keep in mind is the category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
            is a function from the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
          %p For more background on and context for categories see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"}> category theory
              \.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            There are two broad ways to write down the definition of category; in the usual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
          %ul
            %li
              %p Each introduces its own system of notation, both of which are useful in other parts of category theory, so one should know them.
            %li
              %p
                One definition generalises quite nicely to the notion of an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %li
              %p When examining alternative foundations, sometimes one definition or the other may be more appropriate; in any case, one will want to examine the question of their equivalence.
          %p
            The two definitions may be distinguished by whether they use a single collection of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            or several collections of morphisms, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of collections
            indexed by pairs of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
          %h3#OneCollectionOfMorphisms With one collection of morphisms
          %p
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Grothendieck61"}> Grothendieck 61, Section 4
            \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A
            %strong category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
                (see
                %a{:href => "#foundations"} Foundational issues
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#size"} Size issues
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %li
              %p
                a collection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
                of
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                (or
                = succeed ");" do
                  %strong arrows
            %li
              %p
                for every morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(f)
                (called its
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
                or
                = succeed ")," do
                  %strong domain
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f)
                (called its
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
                or
                = succeed ");" do
                  %strong codomain
            %li
              %p
                for every pair of morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = s(g)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} composite
                (also written
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f
                or sometimes
                = succeed "\u2014" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ;
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f;g
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrammatic+order"} diagrammatic order
            %li
              %p
                for every object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_x
                (or
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_x
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %li
              %p such that the following properties are satisfied:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    source and target are respected by composition:
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(g \circ f) = s(f)
                    and
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(g\circ f) = t(g)
                %li
                  %p
                    source and target are respected by identities:
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(1_x) = x
                    and
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi x
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(1_x) = x
                %li
                  %p
                    composition is
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative"} associative
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi h
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                          %mo =
                          %mi h
                          %mo ∘
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h \circ g)\circ f = h\circ (g \circ f)
                    whenever
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = s(g)
                    and
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(g) = s(h)
                %li
                  %p
                    composition satisfies the
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} left and right unit laws
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(f) = x
                    and
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi y
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = y
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi y
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi f
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi x
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_y \circ f = f = f \circ 1_x
          %p
            People also often write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C
            instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C_0
            as a short way to indicate that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
            instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x \to y
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C_1
            to state that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(f) = x
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(x,y)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_C(x,y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y)
            for the collection of morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x \to y
          %p
            If the
            = succeed "-assigning" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicategory"} semicategory
          %h3#AFamilyOfCollectionsOfMorphisms With a family of collections of morphisms
          %p
            A
            %strong category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
                (see
                %a{:href => "#foundations"} Foundational issues
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#size"} Size issues
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %li
              %p
                for each pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
                of objects, a collection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                    from
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                    to
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %li
              %p
                for each pair of morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(y,z)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,z)
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} composite
                (also written
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f
                or sometimes
                = succeed "\u2014" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ;
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f;g
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrammatic+order"} diagrammatic order
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_x
                (or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_x
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,x)
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %li
              %p such that the following properties are satisfied:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    composition is
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative"} associative
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi w
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w,x,y,z
                    of objects, if
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C_1(y,z)
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in C_1(x,y)
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi h
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in C_1(w,x)
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi h
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f \circ g)\circ h = f\circ (g \circ h)
                %li
                  %p
                    composition satisfies the
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} left and right unit laws
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
                    of objects, if
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C_1(x,y)
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi y
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi f
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi x
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_y \circ f = f = f \circ 1_x
          %p
            People also often write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C
            instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C_0
            as a short way to indicate that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C)
            instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(x,y)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_C(x,y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y)
            instead of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x \to y
            to state that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C_1(x,y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \biguplus_{x \in C_0} \biguplus_{y \in C_0} C_1(x,y)
          %h3#equivalence_between_the_two_definitions Equivalence between the two definitions
          %p
            Given a one-collection-of-morphisms category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇉
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1\rightrightarrows C_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t):C_1 \to C_0\times C_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of the families of morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1 = \coprod_{x,y\in C_0} C_1(x,y)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            in both cases, this sets up a strict
            %span.newWikiWord
              2-equivalence
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/2-equivalence"} ?
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
          %p
            Note, though, that this 2-equivalence is not an
            %em isomorphism
            of 2-categories, because the disjoint union operation has to “tag” each morphism with its domain and codomain. It seems that the strongest thing that can be said is that, in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has the property that sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
            are all disjoint, then there is a one-collection-of-morphisms category with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1 = \bigcup_{x,y\in C_0} C_1(x,y)
            (the
            = succeed "-disjoint" do
              %em non
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on the nose. The notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protocategory"} protocategory
            is a way to formalize a family-of-collections-of-morphisms category together with the information about how its hom-sets “overlap”.
          %p
            In ordinary category theory one rarely specifies which of the two definitions is being used, although often language implicitly suggests that it is the latter, e.g. when defining a category one first specifies the objects and then specifies what “the morphisms from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are” rather than specifying what “a morphism” is and then what the domain and codomain of each morphism are. Indeed, when defining a category in this way, one rarely worries about whether the hom-sets are disjoint, meaning that it must be the second definition in use. Even for the prototypical category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a function, i.e. a subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times Y
            that is total and functional”, produces hom-sets that are not disjoint, since a total and functional set of ordered pairs can have any codomain that is a superset of its range. Moreover, categorical constructions do not “naturally” preserve disjointness of homsets, e.g. in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi el
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el(P)
            of a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:C\to Set
            a given morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            can “be” a morphism between many different elements of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            and so on.
          %h3#foundations Foundational issues
          %p
            We said a category has a ‘collection’ of objects and ‘collection’(s) of morphisms. However, different
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+foundations"} mathematical foundations
            have different notions of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            = succeed "-set" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internally
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wild+category"} wild category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precategory"} precategory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            are not strict categories. Instead, they happen to be a special kind of precategory called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
          %h3#size Size issues
          %p
            We said a category has a ‘collection’ of objects and ‘collection’(s) of morphisms. A category is said to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            if these collections are all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            — as opposed to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper classes
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations for mathematics
          %p
            Similarly, a category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
            is a set for every pair of objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
            in that category. The most common motivating examples of categories (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#alternative_definitions Alternative definitions
          %p For some purposes it is useful or necessary to vary the way the ordinary definition of category is expressed. See
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single-sorted+definition+of+a+category"}> single-sorted definition of a category
                – a variant of the first definition, with only
                %em one
                collection at all (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
                , no
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type-theoretic+definition+of+category"}> type-theoretic definition of category
                – a variant of the second definition, interpreted explicitly in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protocategory"}> protocategory
                – a sort of mixture of the two definitions, in which all the hom-sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
                are subsets of a single set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
          %h3#EquivalenceDefinitions Equivalent definitions
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is equivalently
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spans"} spans
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                of endospans on the set of objects;
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                which satisfies the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                which satisfies the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Kan+complex"} weak Kan complex
                conditions strictly:
            %li
              %p
                hence a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+homotopy+type+theory"} directed homotopy type
                which is “1-truncated”
          %h3#generalizations Generalizations
          %h4#internal_categories Internal categories
          %p
            The first definition, with a single collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            of morphisms, generalises to the notion of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as above, with ‘collection’ interpreted as an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            and ‘function’ interpreted as a morphism of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is the same thing as a small category.
          %h4#enriched_categories Enriched categories
          %p
            The second definition of a category, as a family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1(x,y)
            of collections of morphisms, generalises to the notion of an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as above, with the collection of objects still a ‘collection’ as before, but with objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in place of the collections of morphisms and morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in place of the various functions. In particular, a category enriched over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is the same thing as a locally small category.
          %h4#indexed_categories Indexed categories
          %p
            The notion of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
            captures the idea of woking “over a base” other than
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h4#multicategories_etc Multicategories etc.
          %p
            There is a generalization of the notion of a category where one allows a morphism to go from several objects to a single object. This is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %em to
            several objects, we obtain a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polycategory"} polycategory
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PROP"} PROP
          %h4#higher_categories Higher categories
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p This section lists a few well-known categories and some of their properties.
          %p The archetypal example of a category is:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              = succeed "\u2013" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              as objects and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
              as morphisms, and the usual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of functions as composition.
          %p
            Direct generalization of this case are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+categories"} concrete categories
            of sets equipped with
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extract
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            and with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphic
            functions between them as morphisms:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
                as morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
                as morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                as morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+maps"} smooth maps
                as morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
                as morphisms.
          %p
            These all are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+categories"} large categories
          %p
            Yet more generally there are non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"}> concrete categories
            , often
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            ones:
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"} delooping groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              = succeed "\u2013" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary group operation
          %p
            Or for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              = succeed "\u2013" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (its points) and morphisms the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              (relative endpoints) of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            These two are examples of categories which are (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+groupoid"}> small
            )
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+morphisms"} invertible
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            there is its
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                category
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"}>
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}M
              – single object and morphisms the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %p
            and in this vein one may generally regard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
            as being the “monoids with many objects”: the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"}> horizontal categorification
            ” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            (which in the terminology of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oidification"}> oidification
            ” would be called the “monoid-oids” – but are not).
          %p
            In a similar spirit, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered+set"} partially ordered set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \leq)
            it
            %a{:href => "partial+order#AsACategoryWithExtraProperties"} may be regarded
            as a category:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "\u2013" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and with a unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to y
              iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
          %p
            Related to this, while
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graphs"} directed graphs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,E)
            are not themselves categories (lacking a specified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operation and specified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            and in general not even admitting this structure) they induce
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+categories"} free categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(V,E)
              = succeed "\u2013" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
              of the graph and morphisms the sequences of its composable
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
          %p There is no hope (or point) in making a comprehensive list of categories, but here are a few further examples, with comments on their properties:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"}> Ab
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian groups
                as objects, homomorphisms as morphisms. Since this category consists of models of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                it has all small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                and also a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+symmetric+monoidal+category"} closed symmetric monoidal category
                under the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                of abelian groups.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alg"}> Alg
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebras
                as objects, homomorphisms as morphisms. This is actually many different categories, depending on a choice of ground
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                or more generally
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bicat"}> Bicat
                \:
                = succeed "(" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
                = succeed "weak" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
                as its 1-cells,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformations"} pseudonatural transformations
                between its 1-cells as its 2-cells, and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modifications"} modifications
                between its 2-cells as its 3-cells. BiCat is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategory"} tricategory
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"}> CartSp
                \: spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                as objects, smooth maps as morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"}> Cat
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small categories
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functors
                as morphisms. Since this category consists of models of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits+theory"} finite limits theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"}> Diff
                \: smooth
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} Diffeological spaces
                as objects, smooth maps as morphisms. This category has all small limits and colimits, it is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"}> Grp
                \:
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                it has all small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"}>
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
                \: (right)
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                as objects,
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                (or more generally, any small
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                and is thus complete and cocomplete. It is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                and even
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+category"} Grothendieck category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is commutative, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+symmetric+monoidal+category"} closed symmetric monoidal category
                under the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                of
                = succeed "-modules." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-Set"}> M-Set
                \: Category of
                = succeed "-sets," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MultiSet"}> MultiSet
                \: Category of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisets"} multisets
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"}> Rel
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relations
                as morphisms. This is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/allegory"} allegory
                and therefore a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizers
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizers
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"}> Ring
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} rings
                as objects, ring homomorphisms as morphisms. Since this category consists of models of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                it has all small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ring
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring_1
                separately; the difference is important sometimes).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"}> SimpSet
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                as objects, simplicial maps as morphisms. This is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"}> Set
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                as objects,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                as morphisms.
              %p This has the following properties:
              %ul
                %li
                  It is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed
                %li
                  It is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
                %li
                  It is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive
                  (as is any cocomplete topos).
                %li
                  It is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+topos"} well-pointed
              %p
                At least assuming
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                uniquely up to equivalence among all categories. Note, however, that the definitions of “locally small” and “(co)complete” presuppose a notion of
                %em small
                and therefore a knowledge of what a
                %em set
                is.
              %p
                See also
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %span.newWikiWord
                      Understanding Set
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Understanding+Set"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"}> Top
                \:
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category of topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"}> Vect
                \:
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
                when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a field. Since any one of these categories consists of models of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
          %h2#basic_notions Basic notions
          %p
            A homomorphism between categories is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          %p
            This way
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
            themselves form a category, the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            whose objects are small categories and whose morphisms are functors. This naturally enhances to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            whose
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            is an equivalence in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          %p
            Weaker than the notion of a pair of functors exhibiting an equivalence is the notion of a pair of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
          %p Other standard operations on categories include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            %li
